return 1\n    \n    a, b = 0, 1\n    for i in range(2, n + 1):\n        a, b = b, a + b\n    return b\n```\n\n**Time Complexity Analysis:**\n\n1. **Base cases (lines 2–4):** These checks run in constant time, O(1), since they involve simple comparisons and return immediately.\n\n2. **Initialization (line 5):** Assigning two variables takes O(1) time.\n\n3. **Loop (line 6):** The loop runs from 2 to n, executing exactly n - 1 times. Each iteration performs a constant number of operations (assignment and addition), so this part contributes O(n) to the total time.\n\n4. **Return statement (line 7):** Returning a"}
