ating point, biased exponent, 7-bit exponent, 8-bit mantissa. Designed for deep learning (similar to float32 but with less precision in exponent). Good balance of precision and memory.\n    *   **float8:** 8-bit floating point. Two variants: float8_e4m3fn (similar to bfloat16 but half bits) and float8_e5m2. Lower precision, lower memory.\n    *   **Trade-offs:** Precision/Accuracy vs. Memory/Compute Efficiency.\n\n3.  **Drafting the Trade-offs:**\n    *   *Point 1: Memory/Storage.* Float8 uses half the memory of bfloat16. This is a huge win for storage and bandwidth.\n    *   *Point 2: Precision/Accuracy.* Float"}
